A||||7||Carrolles||GT-40 Replica Kits for Fiero???||||5||
Z||000000||Carrolles||06-30-2000||12:54 PM||||I'm interested in building a GT-40 replica on a Fiero.  I saw a nice one at the FOCOA Nationals in St. Louis a couple of years ago.<P>Do any of you have any experience with GT-40 kits?<P>TIA<P>Carroll||||reg||5
Z||000001||dman||06-30-2000||05:00 PM||||Hi Carroll. I've heard the NAF (North American Fiberglass) kit is -the- kit for converting a fiero into a GT40. Unfortunately they don't seem to have a web page. The only internet web page that makes any real reference to that kit that I've found is located here:<BR> <A HREF="http://expert.cc.purdue.edu/~jeverett/gt40kit.html" TARGET=_blank>http://expert.cc.purdue.edu/~jeverett/gt40kit.html</A> <P>I don't know who maintains that site. But I guess it is a student or faculty member (or maybe even an alumni.<P>I believe a member of the Fieros West club built a GT40 using the NAF kit a few years ago. I think he even won a few AHA show awards at the annual Knotts Fun in the Sun show.<P>I saw this car just this past April and it was very nice, unfortunately I did not get a chance to meet the builder.<P>You could probably email WKDFIRO who is a member of this forum and ask him to relay your query to that person. WKDFIRO is president of Fieros West and probably knows that car and builder.<P>Good luck on the rebody should you do it. I can understand your interest since I too considered that rebody. At the moment however I'm working on a Testarossa rebody. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||06-30-2000||07:12 PM||||i emailed that guy, 2 months ago.  i still dont have an answer.<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||06-30-2000||09:21 PM||||I would biuld the GT40 kit<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||cifc||07-01-2000||03:59 PM||||I know a distibutor for the naf kits.  He's a member of our local club (Central Indiana).<BR>His name is Greg and he lives in Louisville.  I'll look for the info and get back.<BR>--Jason<p>[This message has been edited by cifc (edited 07-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-01-2000||04:50 PM||||cifc--Do you ever get over towards Wabash??  If you plan on it, email me.  I'd like to see your car and meet a fellow Fieroholic.<P>OK.  I see you don't have email?  Email me from a library or something.  There are alot of Fieroholics in the general area.  From Auburn to Indy (at least 2 or 3 in Indy area).<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||cifc||07-01-2000||11:02 PM||||I found the flyer.  His number is (502) 245-2472.  If you give him a call tell him Jason from Indiana said hi.<BR>--Jason||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||07-02-2000||05:16 AM||||The person who owns that GT-40 is Dave Hartman. Its a pretty good kit as far as kits go. He has a 3.4 automatic in it and just loves it. I was thinking of him when I was reading the entry. Every once in a while he gets involved with a project and no one heres from him for months at a time. Not only is he a member of Fieros West but he is also a member of a Kit Car club too, (I just can't remember what the name of it is...) <BR>The GT-40 will NEVER pass as the real thing to everyone but its a nice kit that keeps the chassis in one piece and is not so intrusive to regular driving. Perhaps he will resurface at the West Fest. I'll keep my eyes peeled.||||reg||1
